Subject: [PATCH] loop: rescan partitions after changing the block size

LOOP_SET_STATUS64 can enable LO_FLAGS_PARTSCAN before userspace applies
LOOP_SET_BLOCK_SIZE. The initial scan then misses a GPT using 4096-byte
sectors. Rescan after a successful block-size change, once the queue is
unfrozen, as the other loop configuration paths already do.

--- a/drivers/block/loop.c
+++ b/drivers/block/loop.c
@@ -1409,6 +1409,9 @@ static int loop_set_block_size(struct loop_device *lo, unsigned long arg)
 out_unfreeze:
 	blk_mq_unfreeze_queue(lo->lo_queue);
 
+	if (!err && (lo->lo_flags & LO_FLAGS_PARTSCAN))
+		loop_reread_partitions(lo, lo->lo_device);
+
 	return err;
 }
 
